            'To the extent permitted by law, AnyTTY is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages. Any aggregate liability relating to a paid service will not exceed the amount you paid for that service during the twelve months before the event giving rise to the claim. Limits do not apply where prohibited by law.',
          ],
        },
        {
          id: 'changes',
          title: '10. Changes and contact',
          paragraphs: [
            'We may update these terms as the services or legal requirements change. The current version and effective date will remain available here. If applicable law requires consent to a material update, we will request it before the update applies.',
          ],
        },
      ],
    },
    support: {
      title: 'Support',
      description: 'Get help with AnyTTY apps, connections, Cloud accounts, billing, privacy, and security.',
      eyebrow: 'AnyTTY / Support',
      updated: 'Support is available in English and Simplified Chinese.',
      contactTitle: 'Private support',
      contactBody: 'Use email for account, billing, privacy, or other reports that contain private information.',
      email: 'support@anytty.com',
      sections: [
        {
          id: 'setup',
          title: 'Setup and connection help',
          paragraphs: [
            'Start with the public documentation for installation, pairing, Local, SSH, Direct, Cloud, terminal, and file-transfer questions.',
          ],
          links: [
            { label: 'Open quick start', href: '/docs/quick-start/' },
            { label: 'Read connection docs', href: '/docs/connections/' },
          ],
        },
        {
          id: 'bugs',
          title: 'Bug reports and feature requests',
          paragraphs: [
            'Use GitHub for reproducible defects and product proposals after removing credentials, private addresses, terminal output, file content, and customer data. Include the AnyTTY version, operating system, connection type, and steps to reproduce.',
          ],
          links: [
            { label: 'Report a bug', href: 'https://github.com/anytty/anytty/issues/new?template=bug_report.yml', external: true },
            { label: 'Request a feature', href: 'https://github.com/anytty/anytty/issues/new?template=feature_request.yml', external: true },
          ],
        },
        {
          id: 'security',
          title: 'Security vulnerabilities',
          paragraphs: [
            'Do not report security vulnerabilities in a public issue. Use GitHub private vulnerability reporting and provide only the minimum reproduction data needed to investigate.',
          ],
          links: [{ label: 'Report a vulnerability privately', href: 'https://github.com/anytty/anytty/security/advisories/new', external: true }],
        },
        {
          id: 'account',
          title: 'Accounts, billing, and privacy',
          paragraphs: [
            'Email support for sign-in, subscriptions, invoices, cancellation, refunds, App Store purchases, or account-specific questions. Email privacy for access, correction, deletion, or other privacy requests.',
            'Never send passwords, private keys, pairing claims, Cloud tokens, or unredacted terminal and file content.',
          ],
          links: [
            { label: 'Email support', href: 'mailto:support@anytty.com' },
            { label: 'Email privacy', href: 'mailto:privacy@anytty.com' },
          ],
        },
        {
          id: 'availability',
          title: 'Availability',
          paragraphs: [
            'AnyTTY Beta does not include a default response-time or availability SLA. We review reports as capacity allows and prioritize security, data-access, and purchase issues.',
          ],
